## Why This Is Asked
Tests translating CAPA into actionable steps for a concrete, repeatable risk. It targets beginner CAPA skills without vague theory.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model design
- Lifecycle/state machine
- Evidence capture and traceability
- Lightweight REST API for CAPAs
- Canary-based remediation and region-aware metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let cas = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const cap = {...req.body, id: Date.now().toString(), status: 'detected'};
  cas.push(cap);
  res.status(201).json(cap);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the CAPA workflow end-to-end?
- How would you enforce secret masking in build logs across agents?

## Why This Is Asked

Covers a realistic data-leak risk from IAM misconfig in pipelines, focusing on formal CAPA processes at a beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- Lifecycle state machines
- Evidence-driven REST APIs
- Metrics for containment and prevention
- RCA templates and canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Express route to POST /caps
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let caps = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const cap = { id: Date.now().toString(), ...req.body };
  caps.push(cap);
  res.status(201).json(cap);
});
```

